  "summary": "The liquid is enclosed in a flexible hose laid around the inside of the pump housing. Rotating shoes (or rollers) squeeze the hose completely shut and roll the closed point along, pushing the liquid ahead of them; behind the shoe the hose springs back open and draws in more liquid. Only the hose touches the product, there are no seals or valves, and the pump can run dry, self-prime and handle abrasive, viscous and shear-sensitive fluids.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – rotary (peristaltic)",
    "configuration": "Hose pump with two pressing shoes, lubricant-filled housing"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "hose": "Reinforced elastomer hose (NR, NBR, EPDM, CSM)",
    "rotor": "2 shoes; roller versions are used on tube pumps",
    "note": "Hose compression is shown schematically; the real hose is fully occluded under each shoe."
  },
